<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11145" root="خفى" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِخْتَفَى</span></b> , said of a man, [if it be not a mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُخْتُفِىَ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُخْتُفِىَ دَمُهُ</span>,] signifies
also <i>He was slain covertly, secretly,</i> or <i>clandestinely.</i> (JK.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  As a trans. v.: see 1. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  You
say also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اختفى مَيِّتًا</span> <i>He drew forth a dead body</i>

<i>from the grave,</i> to steal the grave-clothes. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اختفى البِئْرَ</span> <i>He dug,</i> or <i>cleared out, the
well.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اختفى دَمَهُ</span> <i>He slew him
without its being known.</i> (K.)

